  "status": "draft",
  "note": "Private test IPA 753, for the maintainer's requests of 15 November 2026 (\"Je vais attendre que tu est corriger tous les d\u00e9fauts Graphique \u00e9galement\", \"corrige bien tout avant la prochaine IPA\") and the logs received that evening (engine.zip, 24 sessions): the verified IPA 752 (run 43756416873, IPA e751a5f5) with the S2Arm engine of patches 0001-0044 (run 43762874022, artifact 14181915479, verified pin cb950b4e). Patches 0040 and 0043: the precompile lookahead and the attachment scan load no shader on the submit thread; Switch 2 stages are translated ahead on a background queue and their libraries loaded on the lanes, so a new scene's shaders are loaded beside the submit thread instead of one after another on it (a real bind still waits for its own). Patches 0041 and 0044: S2Arm's later task / mesh pipeline series, the fragment shader's typed-output variant for a mesh pipeline (the R8Uint refusal found in every race session since 746), M rows only for pipelines that drew. Patch 0042: game threads of core 3 keep the other game threads' tier while the guest's memory is in files (the race start stopped at 0 frames a second on IPA 751 had every game thread waiting for one UTILITY thread blocked in a fault while a screen recording started). Patch 0039, delivered in 752, stays. Not established by the logs: the cause of the objects drawn black and of the vertical colour bands in the recordings of 15 November; a new log line every 300 frames counts skipped first uses so that a later log can be laid beside a recording. The translator's sources are unchanged since IPA 750, so the device's translations and pipeline archive carry over. RPCS3, MeloNX, XeniaCore, the app and every retained component are those of the base; the Nextendo online play session's concurrent commits are source only. Images that must change: S2ArmEngine and Runner. Build-only delivery: Flutter/native groups not-run. Nothing has run on an iPhone; no frame rate, stability or heat claim.",
